<title>USA: US Treasury's Summers - must protect social security.</title>
<headline>US Treasury's Summers - must protect social security.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said fundamental social security benefits must be protected and warned that Americans tend to take them for granted.</p>
<p>&quot;Whatever approach we take going forward, it is absolutely essential to maintain the basic protections that the social security system has provided (and) could continue to provide to Americans as they become aged,&quot; said Summers, responding to a question after addressing an Ernst &amp; Young tax conference in New York.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
